    "notes": "- fix(cs): close the outbound-filter leaks found by backtesting the shadow-mode rules against all 146 historical bot replies\n- New block rules: llm-request-failed (the most common leak — reached a real customer on 2026-08-29) and model-meta (the model narrating its own tooling instead of answering)\n- tool-error now also matches openclaw's tool-failure banner; internal-path and runtime-mention changed from strip to block, because excising a path from machine output left a worse message than the original\n- Backtest after the change: 22 of 146 flagged, all genuine noise, zero false positives — the same 124 real customer replies still pass untouched\n- fix(cs): the cs-event mirror no longer records non-LINE channels, which was filing operator Telegram traffic as a customer conversation",
